  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/621179db-0dfa-4b9e-aed0-91952e7a3eae-image.png\" style=\"width: 339px; height: 166px;\" /><br /><br />Potential difference&nbsp;across each resistor is zero. Hence current is zero in each resistor.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/19e6ec74-6c06-4403-b34e-7425ed0eacd1-image.png\" style=\"width: 360px; height: 186px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence, current through all the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;ressitor is zero.</p>",
